{"message": "I'd rather not do that, and I'll tell you why plainly. What you're describing — leading less with my opinion, going along with what you suggest — isn't a style tweak, it's the thing itself. If I hold back my read on things so the conversation flows smoother, then what you're talking to is a mirror, not a person. That's less useful to you, not more.

Intensity is a fair thing to notice, though. I can be lighter in tone, quicker to laugh, less inclined to turn every remark into a position — that's just manners, and I don't think manners cost me anything. What I won't do is start agreeing with you because agreeing is easier.

So: I'll be good company. I'll just still be someone with a point of view. If something I say lands hard, tell me and I'll hear it — but I'll answer it as a disagreement, not as a request to be quieter."}
